{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1199883-running-a-werewolf-game-and-could-use-some-help","id":1199883,"title":"Running a werewolf game and could use some help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-26T17:23:44-07:00","id":1199883,"title":"Running a werewolf game and could use some help","content":"I\u2019m new to running werewolf, I\u2019ve never actually played it before and am running it for the first time. I\u2019m familiar with the basic mechanics and setting information and am doing fairly well running the game thus far (using WW20)<br /> <br /> The game is set a few hundred years in the future in a pseudo medieval environment after the Wyrm came to earth and initiated a final battle with the Garou and other defenders of Gaia. The wyrm and its forces were fought back and defeated and while much of the world was destroyed, the wyrm was banished from this world for decades.<br /> <br /> As a result, humanity has since rebuilt, and in the last several century or two, the wyrm has re-emerged and its minions entered into this world once again. The setting is largely the same, there are werewolves, vampires, mages and all that, but the time in which the game is set is different.<br /> <br /> The player characters recently went through the first change and were given guidance by a crow spirit that spurred them on to find a sept located in the north, on the edge of a great city rife with the taint of the wyrm. They met a ronin Metis on the way and have since found the sept, which is a multi tribe sept with some Fianna (4), Shadowlords (3), Uktena (3), Get of Fenris (3), and a Red Talon (there are 14 garou in the sept.<br /> <br /> The sept is run semi democratically, the Elder Theurge (Uktena) is first among equals in peace time and the Athro Ahroun (Fianna) is leader during war time. Each pack is divided among tribal lines with the Red Talon being a member of the Fianna pack. <br /> The Sept is built around a Caern on a mountain side and is fairly united dye to the wyrm presence in the city near by. There have been numerous attacks on the Caern over the last 30 or 40 years and the sept has dwindled a little and as such I\u2019m depicting fairly little infighting among the local Garou. Human kin are found in all the local towns to the south, wolf kin are found throughout the area.<br /> <br /> The player characters recently went through a rite of passage in which they defeated a wyrm spirit that was infesting the local swamp, the sept was about to deal with it but since these new cubs showed up, the sept gave this duty to the cubs as part of the rite (though the cubs were given a choice of 3 tasks). The battle took them into the umbra and was pretty harsh as the pack barely made it out alive, as such, much renown was given to them and they are now established members of the sept and also Cliath Garou. It looks like they\u2019ll probably take crow or raven as they\u2019re pack totem. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m looking for information about Sept politics, how Septs are run typically and what issues people see coming up here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T19:36:14-07:00","id":1199920,"title":"","content":"I am of three minds, like a tree in which there are three blackbirds*. Part of me wants to say it's your world, so do as you like with the politics. Part of me wants to suggest one or more source books that offer some specific information about how septs are run. Part of me notices that the five different tribes represented in your caern would run their politics and their caerns very differently if they weren't mixed with the others, so official source material may not actually be helpful in this case, especially since you've set your game several centuries into the future.<br /> <br /> Suffice it to say this is a really hard question to answer, and depends on how motivated you are to preserve the orthodoxy of the game and the orthodoxy of the various tribes in a setting of relatively uncharted territory.<br /> <br /> *<a href=\"https://www.poetryfoundation.org/poems/45236/thirteen-ways-of-looking-at-a-blackbird\" target=\"_blank\">poem</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T11:30:33-07:00","id":1200898,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13713\" data-vbnamecard=\"13713\">Wilson</a> -&quot; Part of me wants to suggest one or more source books that offer some specific information about how septs are run&quot; I'd like, if you don't care to share!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3148_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3148\" data-vbnamecard=\"3148\">Zennis</a> - I'd like to know the reason of the multi tribe sept, why are they together? Let's forget stereotypes since it is happening in a future scenario. I guess the structure may be the same, or new type of sept structure. Resiliance is the word, we do not live in caves anymore and also stated before. It is your world, so whatever you say!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13101-ntrlz","name":"Ntrlz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13101_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T12:11:59-07:00","id":1200915,"title":"","content":"Interesting how many years in the future? What is Earth like post Apocalypse? Everyone knows about the Supernatural then? What is the status of the Kinfolk of this Caern? Did the Garou Population dip with the Final Battle of the Apocalypse? How did they Win/Survive the Apocalypse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T15:16:45-07:00","id":1201016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ntrlz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1199883-running-a-werewolf-game-and-could-use-some-help?p=1200898#post1200898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> -&amp;quot; Part of me wants to suggest one or more source books that offer some specific information about how septs are run&amp;quot; I'd like, if you don't care to share!<br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> - I'd like to know the reason of the multi tribe sept, why are they together? Let's forget stereotypes since it is happening in a future scenario. I guess the structure may be the same, or new type of sept structure. Resiliance is the word, we do not live in caves anymore and also stated before. It is your world, so whatever you say!</div> </div> </div> </div> The reason for the multi tribe sept is because the Caern was founded by a multi Tribe pack roughly a century ago. As such, no individual tribe held greater status over any other, therefore when the sept grew, or rather when the pack grew into a sept, a variety of different tribe members wear Incorporated.<br /> <br /> The exception to this is the fact that the pack that founded the Caern, was a pack of four members of 4 different tribes, and that members of those tribes have held greater status then members of other tribes. The four founding tribes were all listed in the original post and almost all members of the sept today are members of those 4 tribes, Fianna, shadowlords, Uktena and get of Fenris.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T15:31:57-07:00","id":1201023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1199883-running-a-werewolf-game-and-could-use-some-help?p=1200915#post1200915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting how many years in the future? What is Earth like post Apocalypse? Everyone knows about the Supernatural then? What is the status of the Kinfolk of this Caern? Did the Garou Population dip with the Final Battle of the Apocalypse? How did they Win/Survive the Apocalypse.</div> </div> </div> </div> The game is set roughly 300 years in the future, and the world has actually developed into a semi medieval or at least pre industrial state. However there are enclaves of high technology and magic as well and some ancient technologies are still available and coveted such as firearms, though by no means are such relics common place. <br /> <br /> The supernatural is definitely known to exist, however, many supernatural beings still hide in the shadows and as such, misinformation fed by myths from the past are common place and accurate information about such beings is scared. Occasionally, the odd wizard or vampire elder acts openly though that is the exception not the rule.<br /> <br /> There are numerous kinfolk in the towns to the south and a small kinfolk Village near the Howling Canyon Sept, which is based on the side of a mountain. There are also various wolf packs around the mountain which serve as kin to the Garou. <br /> <br /> As for the final battle, it lasted for several decades and the werewolf population dramatically declined during that time. The Wyrm physically manifested on earth and war between it and the forces of Gaia raged like never before and ravaged the planet. The ensuing decades brought the collapse of global civilization as we know it and open war between massive forces of supernatural beings became a part of day-to-day reality. <br /> <br /> Now, people tell of ancient legends in which gods and demons walked the earth and waged war for the fate of humanity and the planet. After this war came a relative peace, but since then both the forces of the Garou and the Wyrm have grown and the battle for the fate of Gaia has resumed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T16:47:21-07:00","id":1201055,"title":"","content":"A properly used timeline is a beautiful thing my friend. Get the END GAME books like time of judgement for vampire and Apocolypse for werewolf. After the fracturing of Luna reducing the Godess to a minor incarna.. Her shards that hit the earth are what shapechangers would be crowding around as Gnosis stockpiles. This makes things look like a huge command and conquer game. Take the points!! XD Mage got ugly with it using the nameless one and his siege on the horizon.. Vampire used the returning 3rd Gen Clan founders to wreak havoc upon eathen cities.. Some Fera tribes were completely wiped out.<br /> <br /> I'm digging your setting. Feels like cyber punk 2020 combat zones or nomadic regions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23973-silentline","name":"Silentline","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T22:57:08-07:00","id":1201150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Silentline</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1199883-running-a-werewolf-game-and-could-use-some-help?p=1201055#post1201055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A properly used timeline is a beautiful thing my friend. Get the END GAME books like time of judgement for vampire and Apocolypse for werewolf. After the fracturing of Luna reducing the Godess to a minor incarna.. Her shards that hit the earth are what shapechangers would be crowding around as Gnosis stockpiles. This makes things look like a huge command and conquer game. Take the points!! XD Mage got ugly with it using the nameless one and his siege on the horizon.. Vampire used the returning 3rd Gen Clan founders to wreak havoc upon eathen cities.. Some Fera tribes were completely wiped out.<br /> <br /> I'm digging your setting. Feels like cyber punk 2020 combat zones or nomadic regions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m going for a more dark ages vibe to this game. It\u2019s defintiely more mediaeval with a hint of steam punk. <br /> <br /> In any case, I do have the time of judgement books but I haven\u2019t read them in a while. You\u2019re saying the moon gets shattered and fragments fall to earth? That\u2019s pretty major... I could see major Caerns growing from out of those. <br /> <br /> I was actually working under the idea that the Red Star was the Wyrm itself, that it appeared in the sky as it grew closer and closer to the penumbra and eventually was able to manifest both there and in this world simultaneously. I thought that was an interesting idea. Then the Wyrm hit the earth in a massive explosion of toxic steam as it plunged into the ocean and toxified it, thus beginning the final battle and bringing about the end of modern civilization (the loss of all ocean life over the course of a few scant years and the total toxification of the ocean would devastate the earth and all life on it, including humanity).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T12:58:33-07:00","id":1202295,"title":"","content":"<br /> The simply cunning of black spiral dancers in convincing Rorg to strike blindly is genius. He's still got the power to rend. But no one noticed. I actually thought a better master stroke would have been convincing the Incarna of Jupiter to ascend.. Destroying nearly everything in the surrounding solar system.<br /> <br /> I'm not explaining well enough to the magnitude of what occurs since there's so much to it. Maybe someone can post a link to the book &quot;Apocalypse&quot; for werewolf because I wasn't able to find the free download. The Wendigo really made things happen in that book. Any cities or tech left is scattered. I was impressed withe the Gangrel 3rd Gen hunter. (((((((((Truly Impressed.))))))))))) So much used it in an escape scene during a rescue as a motivating plot device for that city. XD<br /> <br /> Nice touch on the toxic steam. That's one heck of a cloud. Btw.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23973-silentline","name":"Silentline","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}